cff-version: 1.2.0
title: MineGeoAI-Pre - an offline-first desktop system for multi-scenario land-use prediction in open-pit mining regions
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - name: MineGeoAI-Pre Development Team
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23208511
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-02"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mengzhuoer/MineGeoAI-Pre"
abstract: >-
  MineGeoAI-Pre turns open geodata (CLCD annual land cover, Copernicus DEM,
  Landsat-based spectral indices) into 30 m multi-scenario land-use predictions
  for open-pit mining regions. It runs fully offline on a 4 GB office PC,
  generates the mining land-use class missing from public land-cover products,
  and couples prediction with an offline retrieval-augmented AI assistant.
keywords:
  - land-use change
  - mining
  - cellular automata
  - CLUE-S
  - local LLM
  - reproducibility
